From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tomaszstaniak <68373859+tomaszstaniak@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 01:13:37 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/6] AROS: build and run without Unix-only process, signal and
 network support

Problem: Tokio's process, net and signal features need mio, which has no
AROS backend; rustix has none either, and neither has the open crate.
None of them compiles for AROS, so Helix does not build.
Change: on AROS only, those Tokio features, signal-hook(-tokio), rustix
and open are left out through target-specific dependencies. Code that
starts programs (language servers, debug adapters, formatters, :sh, :pipe)
uses helix_stdx::process, whose spawn reports Unsupported; debug adapters
over TCP report the same; URLs are not opened. Signals are handled as on
Windows (none; in raw mode Ctrl-C is a key). faccess uses std metadata.
getrandom 0.3 gets its custom backend from libc's getentropy. Crossterm
uses its libc backend. The editor runs on a thread with a 16 MiB stack,
since a Shell gives commands 40 KB by default.
Repository: helix-editor/helix
Base: a05c151bb6e8e9c65ec390b0ae2afe7a5efd619b (tag 25.07.1)
Author: tomaszstaniak
Date: 2026-10-19
Platform scope: target_os = "aros" (x86_64 ABIv11); other targets unchanged.
Upstream status: local-only (not submitted).
Verification: built with scripts/hx.py (rust-aros toolchain
aros-helix-20261019); run in Limpet on AROS One 1.3, pool v11-2: opens,
edits and saves files, quits to a working Shell.
Removal: when Tokio (mio) and rustix gain AROS backends.
